  "body": "When `DataTransfer`'s method such as `getData` is called, Safari & Chrome both ignores the charset for the sake of equality at least on Mac. This would mean that, for example, `setData('text/plain; charset=utf-8', 'foo');` is equivalent to `setData('text/plain; charset=Shift_JIS', 'foo');`. Firefox seems to treat these MIME types as distinct types even on Mac.\r\n\r\nGiven there is no mechanism to differentiate text MIME types based on charset on some platforms such as Mac, the spec should allow this behavior.",
